## Phase 4: Development --> Review

**Required artifacts**: Implemented code, passing tests

### Checklist

| # | Requirement | How to verify |
|---|------------|---------------|
| 1 | All acceptance criteria met | Cross-reference each acceptance criterion in the spec against the implementation |
| 2 | Tests are written | Run: `find . -name "*.test.*" -newer docs/specs/<feature>.md` to find new test files |
| 3 | Tests pass | Run: `pnpm nx affected -t test --base=origin/main 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
| 4 | No lint errors | Run: `pnpm nx affected -t lint --base=origin/main 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
| 5 | TypeScript compiles | Run: `pnpm nx affected -t typecheck --base=origin/main 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}
| 6 | Go tests pass | Run: `go test ./... -short -count=1 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
| 7 | Go lint passes | Run: `golangci-lint run ./... 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
{{/ifHasStack}}
{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}
| 6 | .NET builds | Run: `dotnet build --configuration Release 2>&1 \| tail -10` |
| 7 | .NET tests pass | Run: `dotnet test --configuration Release 2>&1 \| tail -20` |
{{/ifHasStack}}
| 8 | Documentation updated | Check if CLAUDE.md, NEXT_STEPS, or SESSION_LOG need updates |
| 9 | Spec matches implementation | If implementation deviated from spec, the spec has been updated |
| 10 | Conventional commits | All commits follow `type(scope): message` format |

### Code quality checks
- No file exceeds size limits (250 TS/TSX{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}, 400 Go{{/ifHasStack}}{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}, 300 C#{{/ifHasStack}})
- No function exceeds 50 lines
- No `console.log`, `any`, or `@ts-ignore` without issue links
{{#ifMultiTenancy config}}
- All queries are tenant-scoped
{{/ifMultiTenancy}}

